> Dear Cristoph,
> I have only a minor comment. I see you're computing the generalized
> inverse and doing matrix multiplication explicitely instead of using
> the common 'lm' or 'lm.fit'. Why is that? Do you find it faster/more
> convenient in any way?

So, that might need discussion indeed. lm/lm.fit sometimes give NAs in the coefficients, ginv never does. The NAs are causing trouble. That's the only reason. Maybe I've overlooked something..

Regards,
Christoph

>
> f.
