>>
>> This seems odd, but I think it is correct. At the beginning of the star
>> function, a test for linearity is performed, which detects that a[1:400] is
>> non-linear, but a[1:500] is linear. Therefore, no fitting is performed for
>> a[1:500] (maybe it would be better to directly fit an AR then, as it is done
>> by ncstar).
>>
>> This seems not to be a problem of the star function, but of the theory
>> behind it. You can try:
>>
>> library(fNonlinear)
>> tnnTest(a[1:400])
>> tnnTest(a[1:500])
>>
>> to see that also the implementation of the test in the fNonlinear package
>> yields this result..
>>
>> Regards,
>> Christoph
